{{!-- components/course-level.hbs — the level badge, from the post's #level-* tag.
     Reusable in the course hero, the buy box and the catalog card. Renders
     NOTHING when no level tag is present, which is deliberate: "no level" is a
     real answer and an "All levels" chip on every untagged course is noise.

     .ns-level is theme-owned (2-components/site-course.css) — dot + mono text,
     the house status vocabulary. The design system has no equivalent; its
     .ns-ccard__level is a POSITION (absolute, inside the card's media), not a
     look, which is why the catalog card passes it in as `class` rather than
     swapping the component out.

     Params
       class  extra classes on the <span> — e.g. `ns-ccard__level` to park the
              badge in the corner of a card's media.

     Context: the current post. --}}
{{#has tag="#level-beginner"}}<span class="ns-level ns-level--beginner {{class}}">{{> icons name="gauge"}}{{t "Beginner"}}</span>
{{else has tag="#level-intermediate"}}<span class="ns-level ns-level--intermediate {{class}}">{{> icons name="gauge"}}{{t "Intermediate"}}</span>
{{else has tag="#level-advanced"}}<span class="ns-level ns-level--advanced {{class}}">{{> icons name="gauge"}}{{t "Advanced"}}</span>{{/has}}
